234RA cQ $|DQ(|a)=200 (2021Wa16)                                                
234RA cQ $S(2n)=9709 {I12} (2021Wa16)                                           
234RA c  1992Bo44: {+238}U(1 GeV p,X). The reaction products were ionized,      
234RA2c  accelerated and transported to moving collectors (tape or rotating     
234RA3c  wheel), passing through a magnetic analyzer. {+234}Ra were identified  
234RA4c  by detecting |b{+-} from daughter {+234}Ac with a HPGe detector (16    
234RA5c  mm diameter) around the collector and analyzing the time behavior.     
234RA6c  High energy part of the |b{+-} spectrum was used for determining the   
234RA7c  lifetime. Similar results by the same group are reported in 1992MeZV,  
234RA8c  1993MeZW, 1990BeZB, 1990MeZQ                                           
234RA  L 0.0          0+                30 S      10                            
234RA2 L %B-=100                                                                
234RA cL $No fission fragments were detected (1992MeZV). An upper limit of      
234RA2cL 1|*10{+-4}% for |b-delayed SF decay branch was given by 1992MeZV.      
234RA cL $From Q(|a) systematics of 2021Wa16, Q(|a)({+234}Ra)<3 MeV.            
234RA2cL Therefore, {+234}Ra is expected to decay predominantly by |b to        
234RA3cL {+234}Ac.                                                              
234RA cL T$|b(t) measurement of 1992Bo44.                                       

