234AC cQ $S(2n)=10456 {I19},  S(2p)=15810 {I20} (2021Wa16)                      
234AC c  1986Gi08: A beam of 11.4 MeV/u {+238}U bombarded a natural             
234AC2c  W({+238}U,X) target at 10 particle nA. The target foils and several    
234AC3c  tantalum foils to stop the reaction products were mounted inside the   
234AC4c  thermal-ion source of the online mass separator. Secondary beams of    
234AC5c  selected mass numbers were collected simultaneously at tape transport  
234AC6c  systems. Each sample was transported from the collector to the         
234AC7c  measuring position, which was equipped with two Ge detectors arranged  
234AC8c  in 180{+o} geometry with a 0.5 mm thick 4|p plastic scintillator in    
234AC9c  between as a |b detector. T{-1/2} was determined from decay curves of  
234ACac  |g-rays and X-rays (known or deduced from known level spacings) from   
234ACbc  daughter nuclei, {+234}Th.                                             
234AC c  2008ChZI: Measured masses of 670 MeV/u {+238}U projectile fragments    
234AC2c  (produced with a {+9}Be target) with time-resolved Schottky Mass       
234AC3c  Spectrometry at GSI. Proposed two long-lived isomers of {+234}Ac at    
234AC4c  140 keV {I30} and 620 keV {I30}, but since these were not discussed    
234AC5c  in the followup publication 2012Ch19, evaluator does not adopt them.   
234AC6c  They also determined T{-1/2} from the number of {+234}Ac ions stored   
234AC7c  in the storage ring as a function of time.                             
234AC  L 0.0                            44 S      7                             
234AC2 L %B-=100                                                                
234AC cL $Only |b{+-} decay has been observed.                                  
234AC cL T$measured by 1986Gi08. Other: 45 s {I2} (2008ChZI).                   
234AC cL $J|p=(1+) was suggested by 1986Gi08 from analogy to {+230}Ac and       
234AC2cL {+232}Ac, and from apparent |b feedings to low-spin states in          
234AC3cL {+234}Th. The 1/2[400] Nilsson state was proposed by 1986Gi08 for      
234AC4cL {+231}Ac and {+233}Ac. A possible configuration for {+234}Ac could     
234AC5cL be: (|p 1/2[400], |n 1/2[631]) 1+.                                     

