234TH    234AC B- DECAY                1986GI08                  26NDS    202601
234TH  H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota$CIT=NDS 207, 351 (2026)$CUT=1-Dec-2023$             
234TH c  1986Gi08: Targets of 45 mg/cm{+2} {+nat}W were bombarded with an 11.4  
234TH2c  MeV/u {+238}U beam to produce secondary beams of {+234}Ac with         
234TH3c  On-line mass-separation techniques at GSI. The secondary beams were    
234TH4c  collected at a tape-transport system and transported to the measuring  
234TH5c  position, which was equipped with two Ge detectors arranged in         
234TH6c  180{+o} geometry with a 0.5 mm thick 4|p plastic scintillator in       
234TH7c  between, used as a |b detector.                                        
234TH c  The partial decay scheme is given as constructed by 1986Gi08.          
234TH c  The total K x-ray intensity expected from K conversion of the          
234TH2c  observed |g-ray transitions, by assuming that the multipolarities of   
234TH3c  the unplaced |g rays are not M3 or higher, is |<24. The fact that the  
234TH4c  measured relative K x-ray intensity of 81 {I11} is much higher than    
234TH5c  the calculated intensity may suggest a presence of some E0             
234TH6c  transitions, and/or M3 (or higher) multipolarity for lower-energy      
234TH7c  unplaced |g rays.                                                      
234TH cG E,RI$Measurements by 1986Gi08.                                         
234TH cG M$From the adopted |gs.                                                
234TH cL J$Adopted values.                                                      
234TH cL E$From E|g.                                                            
234TH c  Due to the incompleteness of the level scheme, no attempt is made to   
234TH2c  deduce absolute normalization or derive |b{+-} feeding intensities.    
