234TH    238U(D,6LI)                   1981JA01                  26NDS    202601
234TH  H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota$CIT=NDS 207, 351 (2026)$CUT=1-Dec-2023$             
234TH c  1981Ja01: E(d)=54.8 MeV. An enge-split pole detector with the          
234TH2c  position-sensitive Si surface barrier focal plane detector was used    
234TH3c  to identify {+6}Li reaction products and analyze the excitation        
234TH4c  spectrum (80 keV FWHM). Absolute reduced |a widths for the             
234TH5c  transitions to the ground-state band members were obtained from        
234TH6c  finite-range distorted-wave analysis. |a intensities and reduced       
234TH7c  hindrance factors deduced from (d,{+6}Li) reaction. |a widths were     
234TH8c  compared with the |a intensities and reduced hindrance factors from    
234TH9c  {+238}U decay. Close agreement between them was interpreted as         
234THac  indicating a predominant direct |a-transfer mechanism in (d,{+6}Li)    
234THbc  reaction.                                                              
234TH c  1980Ja09: Angular distributions were measured. Calculations for        
234TH2c  angular distributions were done with different r(0) parameters, and    
234TH3c  compared with their data.                                              
234TH c  1975Be01: Measured (d,{+6}Li) ground-state cross sections at E(d)=35   
234TH2c  MeV on various targets; the |a-spectroscopic factors were deduced;     
234TH3c  their variations with mass numbers were studied.                       
234TH cL E$From 1981Ja01                                                        
234TH cL E(B,D,E)$Estimated bandhead of a presumed rotational band. No          
234TH2cL attempts were made to resolve the levels within the proposed K=0       
234TH3cL bands.                                                                 
234TH cL J$From 1981Ja01. Angular distributions for transitions to the members  
234TH2cL of the ground-state rotational band were compared by 1981Ja01 to DWBA  
234TH3cL calculations. Although the levels were not fully resolved, the         
234TH4cL individual cross sections for these levels were extracted by using     
234TH5cL peak-fitting procedures. The 2+ state was found to be populated most   
234TH6cL intensely. Assignments to the excited 0+ states were based on          
234TH7cL systematics of 0+ states in the actinide region and on predictions     
234TH8cL from the interacting boson model. Four-point angular distributions     
234TH9cL for transitions to the unresolved levels within the bands were taken.  
234THacL Comparison with DWBA calculations indicated that L=2 is the dominant   
234THbcL component of the unresolved group of levels as was found also for the  
234THccL ground-state band.                                                     
234TH CL BAND(A)$GS BAND. THE 0+ AND 2+ MEMBERS WERE NOT FULLY RESOLVED. The    
234TH2cL energies of 2+ and 4+ levels were taken from previous works; the       
234TH3cL energies of 6+ and 8+ states were estimated by 1981Ja01.               
