234U 4cB 100%. This result (which does not include I|g limits) suggests that    
234U 5cB the |g-ray intensity balance for some levels may be incomplete.        
234U  cG $|b|g: 1962Bj01, 1967Wa26                                              
234U  cG $|g|g: 1986Ar05, 1968Bj06, 1962Bj01                                    
234U  cG $Thirty |g transitions with total photon intensity of 3.2% {I4} have   
234U 2cG not been placed in the decay scheme.                                   
234U  cG $Ice's measured by 1968Bj06 and 1967Wa26 are in fair agreement. Only   
234U 2cG the measurements of 1968Bj06 are given here. The intensities were      
234U 3cG normalized by 1968Bj06 to the integral of the |b{+-} continuum, which  
234U 4cG is defined as 100%. The uncertainties on ce intensities are 20-30% on  
234U 5cG an absolute scale; the relative intensities of the stronger lines may  
234U 6cG be accurate to within 10%, and the weaker ones may be uncertain by as  
234U 7cG much as a factor of 2 (1968Bj06).                                      
234U  cG E$Measurements of 1986Ar05, unless otherwise noted. See also           
234U 2cG 1968Bj06, 1968Go20, 1975Ar24, 1967Wa09, 1967Wa26, and 1964Br24. Early  
234U 3cG measurements: 1954Jo19, 1956On07, 1959De30, 1962Fo11.                  
234U  cG RI$Relative photon intensities, normalized to I(131.3|g)=17.5,         
234U 2cG measured by 1986Ar05 are given here. See also 1990Sc09, 1968Bj06,      
234U 3cG 1975Ar24, 1968Go20, 1967Wa09, 1967Wa26. Relative intensities in        
234U 4cG 1968Bj06 were normalized by the authors using experimental Ice and     
234U 5cG I|g and theoretical conversion coefficients.                           
234U  cG RI$When the photon intensity of a transition is expected to be much    
234U 2cG weaker than the other component(s) of a multiply placed |g ray, and    
234U 3cG its intensity could not be estimated realistically, then no intensity  
234U 4cG is given for such weak component.                                      
234U  cG M$From ce measurements of 1968Bj06, 1967Wa26, 1964Br24. See also       
234U 2cG {+234}Np |e decay, 1.159-min {+234}Pa |b{+-} decay and {+238}Pu |a     
234U 3cG decay. Multipolarities in square brackets have not been                
234U 4cG experimentally determined, they are expected from decay scheme. If M1  
234U 5cG and E2 admixtures are expected, the multipolarity is presented as      
234U 6cG [M1+E2]; however, if M1 and/or E2 multipolarities are possible, then   
234U 7cG the |g-ray multipolarity is presented as [M1,E2].                      
