234U  cG $Because of the coincidence observed with a 946-keV |g-ray gate,       
234U 2cG 1986Ar05 placed this transition also between the 4+ level at 1882 keV  
234U 3cG and the 3- level at 1722 keV. Considering the main configurations of   
234U 4cG the 1882- and 1722- keV levels, a |g-ray transition between them       
234U 5cG should be forbidden. Although probable configuration mixings in        
234U 6cG either or both levels would permit the transition, its intensity       
234U 7cG (being proportional to the square of mixing amplitude) would be quite  
234U 8cG weak. An alternative explanation for the observed 159|g-946|g          
234U 9cG coincidence may be a possible 67.2|g connecting the 1261-keV and       
234U acG 1194-keV levels.                                                       
