234U     233U(D,P)                     1968BJ05                  26NDS    202601
234U   H TYP=FUL$AUT=S. Ota$CIT=NDS 207, 351 (2026)$CUT=1-Dec-2023$             
234U  c  1968Bj05: An enriched (98.06%) {+233}U target (on a carbon backing)    
234U 2c  was irradiated at E(d)=13 MeV. The proton spectra from (d,p) were      
234U 3c  measured at 90|' and 125|' with a broad-range single-gap magnetic      
234U 4c  spectrograph and recorded on photographic plates. The energy           
234U 5c  resolution was about 14 keV.                                           
234U  c  Q(d,p)=4656 {I15} (1968Bj05) and 4520 {I30} (1961Ho12). 4621 keV from  
234U 2c  2021Wa16 (calculated by evaluator).                                    
234U  c  1961Ho12: A {+233}U target was bombarded with 10.7 MeV deuterons.      
234U 2c  Protons from (d,p) reactions were detected by CsI behind a magnetic    
234U 3c  spectrograph.                                                          
234U  cL J$J|p and configuration assignments of 1968Bj05 are based on           
234U 2cL spectroscopic factors (ratio of observed to calculated cross           
234U 3cL sections) at |q=90|' and 125|'. See 1968Bj05 for the optical-model     
234U 4cL parameters used in DWBA calculations. Assignments given to various     
234U 5cL bands are from the contributing two-neutron configurations: odd        
234U 6cL neutron in {+233}U + added neutron state. Squared amplitudes of these  
234U 7cL configurations in collective states are given when they were deduced   
234U 8cL experimentally.                                                        
234U  cL E$From 1968Bj06 unless otherwise noted. About 14 keV overall energy    
234U 2cL resolution (1968Bj05). > 50 keV resolution for 1961Ho12.               
234U  cL E(B)$Line is broader than expected for a single level.                 
