234U  c  1968Bj05: An enriched (>99.8%) {+235}U target (on a carbon foil        
234U 2c  backing) was irradiated at E(d)=13 MeV. The triton spectrum from       
234U 3c  (d,t) was measured at 90|' and 125|' with a broad-range single-gap     
234U 4c  magnetic spectrograph and recorded on photographic plates. The energy  
234U 5c  resolution was about 9 keV.                                            
234U  c  Q(d,t)=935 {I15} (1968Bj05). Note 992 keV from 2021Wa16 (calculated    
234U 2c  by evaluator). The authors discussed possible deviations from other    
234U 3c  Q(d,t) values (997 {I30} and 968 keV). This may be a reason that the   
234U 4c  reported level energies are slightly off from other measurements       
234U 5c  (e.g., 1968Bj05 and Adopted Levels).                                   
234U  cL J$J|p and configuration assignments of 1968Bj05 are based on           
234U 2cL spectroscopic factors (ratio of observed to theoretical (DWBA) cross   
234U 3cL sections) at |q=90|' and 125|'. See 1968Bj05 for the optical-model     
234U 4cL parameters used in DWBA calculations. Assignments given to various     
234U 5cL bands are from the contributing two-neutron configuration to the       
234U 6cL state. Squared amplitudes of these configurations in collective        
