234U  c  {+234}U(|m{+-},F): muon momentum=39 MeV/c (1990Ha03); lifetime for     
234U 2c  muon bound in 1s orbital was measured by 1990Ha03 to be |t=70.6 ns     
234U 3c  {I2}. No longer (about second) component, corresponding to a SF        
234U 4c  isomer, was observed by 1990Ha03.                                      
234U  c  {+234}U(e,e'F): E=5-7 MeV (1986Ar02), E=5.5-25.4 MeV                   
234U 2c  (1982Ar14,1981Ar09); the electrofission cross sections were measured;  
234U 3c  giant quadrupole and giant dipole resonance-parameters, and            
234U 4c  transition strengths were deduced.                                     
234U  c  {+234}U(|g,F): E=5-18 MeV (1986Be38); from measured cross sections,    
234U 2c  giant dipole resonance parameters were deduced.                        
234U  c  {+234}U(n,n'F): E=2.6-4.7 MeV (1983Dm04); searched for a fissioning    
234U 2c  isomer and upper limits for its production cross sections were given   
234U 3c  by 1983Dm04 as between 1.5|*10{+-6} b, for T{-1/2}|?100 ns and         
234U 4c  2|*10{+-5} b, for T{-1/2}=20 ns.                                       
234U  c  {+234}U(n,n'F): E=5-11 MeV (1987Go36); influence of angular momentum   
234U 2c  on the fission probability was observed and results were discussed by  
234U 3c  1987Go36 in terms of two-hump-fission barrier.                         
234U  c  {+233}U(d,pF): E=13 MeV (1971Ba30,1974Ba28); the fission probability   
234U 2c  was deduced from the measured singles rates and the measured triple    
234U 3c  coincidences between fission fragments and protons. Fission-barrier    
234U 4c  parameters were extracted by 1974Ba28.                                 
234U  c  {+233}U(d,pF): E=11, 12.5, 13 MeV (1986Bl11); fission probability and  
234U 2c  fission-fragment angular distributions were measured and observed      
234U 3c  fine structure is discussed in 1986Bl11. See also 1978Go13, 1982Pa14,  
234U 4c  1989AnZO, 1999Kr18, and 2001Kr05, for (d,pF) data and discussions.     
234U  c  {+233}U(d,pF): E=12 MeV (1998Kr19, 1999Kr16, 1999Kr18, 2001Kr17,       
234U 2c  2006KrZY); Measured protons in coincidence with fission fragments.     
234U 3c  Deduced hyperdeformed states in {+234}U. The g.s. in the third         
234U 4c  minimum of the potential energy well was estimated to be at 3.1 MeV    
234U 5c  {I4}.                                                                  
234U  c  {+233}U(n,F): see 1981Wa05, 1983Be05, 1983Go20, 1986Go09, 1986Ga28,    
234U 2c  1988Ba73, 1993Fl01, 1997Ba83, 1994Le31, 1994Le01, and 1994Gu02.        
234U  c  {+232}Th({+16}O,{+14}Cf): see 1987Vi02, 2000Si04, and 2000MeZZ.        
234U  c  {+232}Th(|a,2nF): 2005ThZZ, 2004ThZZ, 1998Er01, 1997Er02, 1995ErZY,    
234U 2c  1995Er03, and 1994ErZZ.                                                
234U  c  {+236}U(p,tF): 2012Hu01. A 28 MeV proton beam on a {+236}U target.     
234U 2c  Measured E(t) and fission energy spectra in coincidence with a Si      
234U 3c  telescope array, and measured coincident |g-rays with a                
234U 4c  Compton-suppressed Ge array. |s[{+234}U(n,F)]/|s[{+233}U(n,F)] ratio   
234U 5c  was measured at neutron energies from nearly 0 MeV to 8 MeV with the   
234U 6c  surrogate ratio method using (p,dF) and (p,tF) reactions on the        
234U 7c  {+236}U target.                                                        
234U  c  {+233}U(d,pF|g): 2017Ro16. A 12.5 MeV deuteron beam on a {+233}U       
234U 2c  target. A Si telescope measured protons (at backward angle) while      
234U 3c  PPAC detectors measured fission fragments (at forward angle). A NaI    
234U 4c  array measured coincident |g-rays. Prompt fission |g spectra were      
234U 5c  measured as a function of {+234}U excitation energy from 4.8 to 10     
234U 6c  MeV.                                                                   
234U  c  {+237}Np({+18}O,{+21}F){+234}U: 2020Ve07. Fission fragment spectra     
234U 2c  were measured at the {+234}U excitation energies between 7-60 MeV,     
234U 3c  using a {+18}O beam on a {+237}Np target at 162 MeV. {+234}U           
234U 4c  excitation energy was deduced by a Si telescope array and the fission  
234U 5c  fragment energy was measured with four multi-wire proportional         
234U 6c  counters. The fission spectra were measured in                         
234U 7c  {+232}Th({+18}O,{+16}C){+234}U reaction by the same group (2016Le13).  

